{"name":"Eagle Ridge","hex":"#7d776c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eagle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several large carnivorous and carrion-eating birds in the family Accipitridae, having a powerful hooked bill and keen vision.","A gold coin with a face value of ten dollars, formerly used in the United States."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To score an eagle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eagle"},{"term":"ridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The back of any animal; especially the upper or projecting part of the back of a quadruped.","Any extended protuberance; a projecting line or strip."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form into a ridge.","To extend in ridges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eagle Ridge, Calgary","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle Ridge is an affluent residential neighbourhood situated on a peninsula in the Glenmore Reservoir in the southwest quadrant of Calgary, Alberta, Canada. The community is known for its unique proximity to green spaces and parks, recreational waterways, and Calgary's multi-use urban pathway system despite its relative proximity to the city's denser downtown core and adjoining communities. In 2014, Eagle Ridge was ranked the 18th wealthiest neighbourhood in Canada and 3rd wealthiest in Calgary. One of Calgary's smallest neighbourhoods by population, Eagle Ridge is physically secluded from other nearby communities due to the Glenmore Reservoir acting as natural boundary to its north, west, and south, while 14 Street W bounds the community to the east."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Ridge%2C_Calgary"},{"title":"Eagle","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle is the common name for certain large predatory birds of prey within the family of the Accipitridae. While on a genetic level, only the subfamily Aquilinae comprises \"true eagles\", many other species are commonly referred to as eagles, such as the bald eagle, and the term generally carries no taxonomic weight. Most of the 68 species of eagles are from Eurasia and Africa. Outside this area, just 14 species can be found—two in North America, nine in Central and South America, and three in Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Eagles_together.jpg/330px-Eagles_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle"},{"title":"Ridge","blocks":[{"text":"A ridge is a long, narrow, elevated geomorphologic landform, structural feature, or a combination of both separated from the surrounding terrain by steep sides. The sides of a ridge slope away from a narrow top, the crest or ridgecrest, with the terrain dropping down on either side. The crest, if narrow, is also called a ridgeline. Limitations on the dimensions of a ridge are lacking. Its height above the surrounding terrain can vary from less than a meter to hundreds of meters. A ridge can be either depositional, erosional, tectonic, or a combination of these in origin and can consist of either bedrock, loose sediment, lava, or ice depending on its origin. A ridge can occur as either an isolated, independent feature or part of a larger geomorphological and/or structural feature. Frequently, a ridge can be further subdivided into smaller geomorphic or structural elements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg/330px-%E4%B8%AD%E6%A9%AB%E5%85%AC%E8%B7%AF%E7%9C%BA%E6%9C%9B%E6%A2%A8%E5%B1%B1%E5%8F%8A%E9%9B%AA%E5%B1%B1%E5%8D%97%E7%A8%9C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Old_Abe%2C_the_live_war_eagle_of_Wisconsin%2C_from_the_Centennial.jpg?utm_sou